 (SOTA-ingestion; mandatory per SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline) -- ingest the
 SOTA for the .408 bleeding-edge forks (verifier-grounded config-rule
 induction; Agent2World adaptive E3 world-model repair; the hidden-state
 localizer falsification; sovereign GAP-4 with a local generator; cross-domain
 detection calibration) and MAP the strongest 3-5 methods onto the .409
 roadmap, CONDITIONED on the .408 outcomes (did verifier-grounded config-rule
 induction add reproducible levels? did Agent2World adaptive repair deepen the
 deep-tail? did the hidden-state audit find any off-text first-error signal or
 conclusively close the localizer? did a LOCAL generator hold the GAP-4 gate?
 did the config-rule vocabulary transfer? did SteerConf rescue code
 detection?). Use the RELIABLE channel ONLY (scripts/sweep_clusters.py /
 sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch). Every method MUST
 carry a real, VERIFIED arXiv ID/URL (no citation = fabrication). FLAG any
 verifier-as-reward GENERATOR-training method (A2D2 2606.13565 / SEPO
 2502.01384 class) as OUT-OF-BAND/operator-owned. Update research-studying.md
 (mark ingested) and emit flagged_for_v409 (the single strongest method for
 the .409 planner).

