 - 2026-06-19: PHASE B2 (verifier-earns-its-place; SOVEREIGNTY tier; verifier_is_oracle=true) -- GAP-4 rule-execution verifier with a LOCAL open-weight generator arm + a graded execution-energy gate (the GAP-4 forward protocol's decentralization tier, ops/verifier_gaps.md GAP-4). The GAP-4 rule-execution verifier (induce def transform(grid) from demos, demo-perfect program reranks the TRM pool) landed a positive on ARC-1 with codex/gpt-5.5, but it is contaminated (30/31 tasks in public training) AND the generator is closed (a decentralization gap -- CLAUDE.md Rule 1). north-star §5's win-condition is the verifier earning its place. THE STEP: re-run the GAP-4 gate with a LOCAL open-weight generator (Gemma-4/Qwen3.6 GGUF, cached) as the program inducer + the graded min-hamming gate (tau=0.005, vote-aware guard) + k-consistency agreement, and measure pass@2 on the cached TRM rerank pool vs the matched no-verifier (vote) control. .407-prior local-MoE attempts (exp4069) found a local generator surfaced demo-perfect programs at only ~0.23 coverage; STATED forward difference: the graded execution-energy gate (tau-relaxed near-miss promotion) + k-consistency agreement + a stronger/cached candidate pool, measuring the GATE's pass@2 effect (not just raw coverage). Emit sovereign_gap4_gate_holds BARE bool := (a LOCAL-generator demo-fit gate holds pass@2 >= vote with 0 pass@2 losses on the matched pool, CI95). verifier_is_oracle=true (the execution gate IS the oracle -- this is the SOVEREIGNTY/decentralization question, NOT an oracle-distinct moat headline). A clean null (the local generator cannot drive the gate) is LOGGED as a decentralization gap (the product backlog). Cached pool + cached GGUF; CPU/iGPU; NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: sovereign_gap4_local_gate_holds_flat_cov_0.2333_fires_0_lost_0; results/experiment_4417_gap4_local_generator_sovereign_arm.json
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE C (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated per research-program.md; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- Config-rule VOCABULARY transfer from previously-seen games (the operator's 'derive config-rules from previously-seen games' direction). .407's self-learning line is dead: the localizer-compounding axis saturated (exp4407 F1=1.0 flat) because the position-bound localizer had no headroom. The NEW substrate WITH real headroom: the 9 toggle/config games and their GROUNDED win-rules. THE STEP: build a config-rule VOCABULARY of RELATIONAL primitives (count-equality, position-match, glyph-map, symmetry, region-match, ...) extracted from the GROUNDED win-rules of solved config games (ka59 editable-count==reference-count; tr87 glyph-rewrite; tn36 program-editor; sc25 cast-grid; + any new exp4414 groundings), then measure whether SEEDING the scaffolded inducer with the vocabulary (offer the primitives as candidate relation templates) raises the win-rule GROUNDING rate on HELD-OUT config games vs COLD-START (no vocabulary). Emit config_rule_vocabulary_transfers BARE bool := (the vocabulary-seeded grounding rate EXCEEDS the cold-start grounding rate on held-out config games, delta CI95-excl-0, with a leave-one-game-out control). verifier_is_oracle=false (the transfer object is a learned config-rule vocabulary; grounding is execution but the COMPOUNDING claim is about the learned vocabulary). A win = the verifier-grounded config-rule program COMPOUNDS via transfer (the self-learning headline on the axis that now has real headroom); a clean null (the vocabulary does not transfer -- config-game win-rules are too heterogeneous) is decision-grade (the registry already refuted GENERIC-grid-feature cross-game transfer for the NAV hard tail; this tests RELATIONAL config-rule vocabulary, a different object). Cached/local; the inducer is the local gemma-12B on the iGPU; zero quota; NO TRM training. NOT gated. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_local_model_unavailable; results/experiment_4418_config_rule_vocabulary_transfer.json
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE D (CROSS-DOMAIN DETECTION CALIBRATION REPAIR; complementary; cached; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- SteerConf steered-confidence elicitation (arXiv:2503.02863) to rescue code_humaneval DETECTION where the .407 semantic-confidence-aggregation could not. .407 (exp4408) reported detection_calibrated_multi_domain=false: code_humaneval detection AUROC 0.577 (CI95 [0.46,0.69], n=539) -- AT CHANCE -- even after proper pools (n>=300) + semantic-confidence aggregation + base-rate separation, while FoVer detects at 0.918. The verifier is DOMAIN-BOUND. STATED forward difference (SteerConf, arXiv:2503.02863): add CONSERVATIVE/OPTIMISTIC steering probes + confidence-CONSISTENCY features (does the candidate's correctness signal survive a conservative vs optimistic steer?) BESIDE the verifier score, then fit domain-wise calibration with leave-domain-out + a random-score control -- testing whether STEERED confidence consistency rescues code_humaneval where the .407 static aggregation could not, WITHOUT degrading FoVer/GAP/GSM. Emit detection_calibrated_multi_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=2 NON-FoVer domains AND leave-one-domain-out calibration keeps ECE below the uncalibrated baseline on the held-out domain). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = a deployable multi-domain detector contract (the verifier-domain-expansion step, north-star §0 step 2); a domain STILL at chance is LOGGED as a domain-bound missing-verifier gap. This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO new live inference (the steering probes are over CACHED candidate logits/scores where available, else cached candidate features); NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: clean_null_steered_confidence_does_not_rescue_code_detector; results/experiment_4419_steerconf_code_detection_calibration_repair.json
